# Secrets. `.env` holds the YouTube API key; any copy or backup of it is a
# secret too. Only the template is committed.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Downloaded media and everything derived from it at full size (academic use
# only, never redistributed). Includes data/_thumbnails.
data/

# Pipeline outputs. The saved reports and their written analyses ARE committed:
# they are what the Library opens on a fresh checkout. Half-written files from
# the atomic writes are not.
outputs/*.csv
*.tmp
*.part

# Derived video frames: only those of the committed reports and set members
# (README, "Frames in the repository"). They are committed once, as built into
# interface/static/frames, which the server reads without a build step. Their
# source, interface/ui/public/frames (written by interface/ui_build/build_frames.py,
# copied into interface/static/ by `npm run build`), stays local.
# interface/static/frames also collects run-time cache (frame_cache.py) for every
# video ever opened, which is not committed. Adding a report to the repository
# means adding its video id to the list below, then running
# interface/ui_build/build_frames.py and `npm run build`.
interface/ui/public/frames/
interface/static/frames/*
